Requirements:
In addition to the general application requirements, applicants to the M.A., Ed.M., and Ed.D. programs in Adult Learning & Leadership must also submit the following:

A resume is required.

Statement of Purpose: Please describe in 3-5 pages (double-spaced) your reasons for applying to the Adult Learning and Leadership Program. You should include the following in your statement:

- Major personal and professional accomplishments and how they have prepared you for this program;
- Your reasons for applying for the particular degree program for which you have applied (M.A., Ed.M., or Ed.D.);
- Specific TC faculty members you would like to work with and why;
- Specific questions you would like to explore in the program;
- Your professional objectives and how this degree will help you to achieve them.

Writing Sample: Please submit a written piece that you feel is the best representation of your ability to write for a graduate-level program. Submissions should be no longer than 15 pages in length and can include a paper from a previous course of study, professional report, or an article for publication. If you do not have a piece of writing that fits this description, please write a 10-15 page paper describing a significant learning experience that you designed or facilitated. Describe the learners, the desired outcomes, the context, and the rationale for the strategies you used. Reflect on the outcomes, both intended and unintended, and what you would do differently in the future.

Standardized test scores (e.g., GRE or GMAT) are not required for admission to our programs.
